    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d736">

                <pb facs="0809" n="801" sameAs="frus:frus1939v05/pg801"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3331/283c: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Wilson</hi>)<anchor n="16" xml:id="d736-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1939-10-21">October 21,
                        1939</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Notice of intention to negotiate a trade agreement with Uruguay was issued here
                        today<anchor n="17" xml:id="d736-f2"/> and the Legation at Montevideo is
                    being instructed to initiate general provisions discussions with the Uruguayan
                    officials at once. You will probably wish to discuss this matter fully with
                    Fowler as the Embassy at Buenos Aires is being instructed to have him assist the
                    Legation in such discussions to the extent permitted by the work in Buenos
                    Aires.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Cordell Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d736-f1" n="16" type="source" xml:id="d736-f1-content">
                <p>Mr. Wilson was en route to his post aboard the S. S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Uruguay</hi>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d736-f2" n="17" xml:id="d736-f2-content">
                <p>Department of State <hi rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, October 21, 1939, p.
                    418.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
